Section: Requests and JSON

 `is-html-builtin` binds these four, and TheShimmeringPortal lists them
 as part of this contract, but no typed stub was ever written for them.
 A chapter that called one therefore could not compile, so every app
 that wanted them declared its own copy -- which is what the stub
 contract exists to prevent, and what the CDX3006 collisions between
 the app themes are. The signatures match the MAUI plug's stubs
 (`codex/plugs/maui/MauiStubs.codex`), which are the same contract for
 the other backend.

  fetch-then : Text, Text, Text, (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  fetch-then (url) (method) (body) (cb) = 0
  json-parse-obj : Text -> List Text
  json-parse-obj (s) = []
  json-obj-field : List Text, Text -> Text
  json-obj-field (obj) (key) = ""
  url-encode : Text -> Text
  url-encode (s) = s
  fetch-json : Text, Text, Text -> DomElement
  fetch-json (url) (method) (body) = dom-null
  json-parse : Text -> List (List Text)
  json-parse (s) = []
  json-stringify : Text -> Text
  json-stringify (s) = s

